  ],
  "sections": [
    {"id":"sec-whitepaper-1","title":"Strata","level":1,"document":"doc-whitepaper","order":1,"body":"\nStrata is a multi-tenant automation and content platform in which every tenant has a database of its own. Tenant structure is versioned data interpreted by one pure kernel. The platform is built so that agents can observe, explain and change it through the same typed, authorised operations people use, with every change simulated before it is applied and recorded after.\n\nThis paper says what the platform is for, where its boundaries are, what was decided and what is still open. The requirements derived from it are in the files the [specification index](../index.md) lists, and the order of work is in the [roadmap](roadmap.md).\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-whitepaper-2","title":"Goals","level":2,"document":"doc-whitepaper","order":2,"body":"\nEach goal is tagged with the release stage that verifies it.\n\n**Tenancy**\n\n{{entity:g-1}}\n{{entity:g-2}}\n{{entity:g-3}}\n{{entity:g-4}}\n{{entity:g-5}}\n\n**Identity**\n\n{{entity:g-6}}\n{{entity:g-7}}\n{{entity:g-8}}\n{{entity:g-9}}\n{{entity:g-10}}\n{{entity:g-11}}\n{{entity:g-12}}\n{{entity:g-46}}\n\n**Automation**\n\n{{entity:g-13}}\n{{entity:g-14}}\n{{entity:g-15}}\n{{entity:g-16}}\n{{entity:g-17}}\n{{entity:g-47}}\n\n**Delivery**\n\n{{entity:g-18}}\n{{entity:g-19}}\n{{entity:g-20}}\n{{entity:g-21}}\n{{entity:g-22}}\n\n**Agents**\n\n{{entity:g-23}}\n{{entity:g-24}}\n{{entity:g-25}}\n{{entity:g-26}}\n{{entity:g-27}}\n{{entity:g-28}}\n\n**Observability**\n\n{{entity:g-29}}\n{{entity:g-30}}\n\n**Content**\n\n{{entity:g-31}}\n{{entity:g-32}}\n{{entity:g-33}}\n{{entity:g-34}}\n{{entity:g-35}}\n\n**Platform**\n\n{{entity:g-36}}\n{{entity:g-37}}\n{{entity:g-38}}\n{{entity:g-39}}\n{{entity:g-40}}\n\n**Assurance**\n\n{{entity:g-41}}\n{{entity:g-42}}\n{{entity:g-43}}\n{{entity:g-44}}\n{{entity:g-45}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-whitepaper-3","title":"Non-goals","level":2,"document":"doc-whitepaper","order":3,"body":"\n{{entity:ng-1}}\n{{entity:ng-2}}\n{{entity:ng-3}}\n{{entity:ng-4}}\n{{entity:ng-5}}\n{{entity:ng-6}}\n{{entity:ng-7}}\n{{entity:ng-8}}\n{{entity:ng-9}}\n{{entity:ng-10}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-whitepaper-4","title":"Boundaries","level":2,"document":"doc-whitepaper","order":4,"body":"\nEvery interface a requirement can be stated at. A requirement names one of these and the surface it is observed through.\n\n{{entity:b-1}}\n{{entity:b-2}}\n{{entity:b-3}}\n{{entity:b-4}}\n{{entity:b-5}}\n{{entity:b-6}}\n{{entity:b-7}}\n{{entity:b-8}}\n{{entity:b-9}}\n{{entity:b-10}}\n{{entity:b-11}}\n{{entity:b-12}}\n{{entity:b-13}}\n{{entity:b-14}}\n{{entity:b-15}}\n{{entity:b-16}}\n{{entity:b-17}}\n{{entity:b-18}}\n{{entity:b-19}}\n{{entity:b-20}}\n{{entity:b-21}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-whitepaper-5","title":"Components","level":2,"document":"doc-whitepaper","order":5,"body":"\nThe components of the platform. Their relationships, the records they own and the copies they hold are modelled in the same specification file and drawn by Exegra.\n\n{{entity:kernel}}\n{{entity:substrate}}\n{{entity:store-contract}}\n{{entity:sqlite-adapter}}\n{{entity:postgres-adapter}}\n{{entity:tenant-database}}\n{{entity:control-plane}}\n{{entity:control-database}}\n{{entity:identity-service}}\n{{entity:runtime}}\n{{entity:gateway}}\n{{entity:automation-worker}}\n{{entity:connector-runner}}\n{{entity:copy-store}}\n{{entity:file-store}}\n{{entity:delivery-network}}\n{{entity:agent-gateway}}\n{{entity:telemetry-pipeline}}\n{{entity:audit-log}}\n{{entity:key-service}}\n{{entity:mail-service}}\n{{entity:external-identity-provider}}\n{{entity:web-application}}\n{{entity:simulator}}\n{{entity:verification}}\n{{entity:agent}}\n{{entity:notice-queue}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-whitepaper-6","title":"Decisions","level":2,"document":"doc-whitepaper","order":6,"body":"\n{{entity:d-1}}\n{{entity:d-2}}\n{{entity:d-3}}\n{{entity:d-4}}\n{{entity:d-5}}\n{{entity:d-6}}\n{{entity:d-7}}\n{{entity:d-8}}\n{{entity:d-9}}\n{{entity:d-10}}\n{{entity:d-11}}\n{{entity:d-12}}\n{{entity:d-13}}\n{{entity:d-14}}\n{{entity:d-15}}\n{{entity:d-16}}\n{{entity:d-17}}\n{{entity:d-18}}\n{{entity:d-19}}\n{{entity:d-20}}\n{{entity:d-21}}\n{{entity:d-22}}\n{{entity:d-23}}\n{{entity:d-24}}\n{{entity:d-25}}\n{{entity:d-26}}\n{{entity:d-27}}\n{{entity:d-28}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-whitepaper-7","title":"Constraints","level":2,"document":"doc-whitepaper","order":7,"body":"\n{{entity:k-1}}\n{{entity:k-2}}\n{{entity:k-3}}\n{{entity:k-4}}\n{{entity:k-5}}\n{{entity:k-6}}\n{{entity:k-7}}\n{{entity:k-8}}\n{{entity:k-9}}\n{{entity:k-10}}\n{{entity:k-11}}\n{{entity:k-12}}\n{{entity:k-13}}\n{{entity:k-14}}\n{{entity:k-15}}\n{{entity:k-16}}\n{{entity:k-17}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-whitepaper-8","title":"Open questions","level":2,"document":"doc-whitepaper","order":8,"body":"\nNo question is open. Each one that was raised is now a decision, listed under Settled questions.\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-roadmap-1","title":"Roadmap","level":1,"document":"doc-roadmap","order":1,"body":"\nMilestones are in dependency order: each one builds on the seams of the ones before it. The first slice a customer can buy ends with milestone 6: sign-up and roles come from milestone 3, review and notices from milestone 5, and authoring, delivery and billing usage from milestone 6. Nothing here says how long anything takes.\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-roadmap-2","title":"Release stages","level":2,"document":"doc-roadmap","order":2,"body":"\n{{entity:r0}}\n\n{{entity:r1}}\n\n{{entity:r2}}\n\n{{entity:r3}}\n\n{{entity:r4}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-roadmap-3","title":"RM-1 Gate","level":2,"document":"doc-roadmap","order":3,"body":"\n{{entity:rm-1}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-roadmap-4","title":"RM-2 Tenant databases and seams","level":2,"document":"doc-roadmap","order":4,"body":"\n{{entity:rm-2}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-roadmap-5","title":"RM-3 Identity core","level":2,"document":"doc-roadmap","order":5,"body":"\n{{entity:rm-3}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-roadmap-6","title":"RM-4 Federation and tokens","level":2,"document":"doc-roadmap","order":6,"body":"\n{{entity:rm-4}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-roadmap-7","title":"RM-5 Scheduling and workflows","level":2,"document":"doc-roadmap","order":7,"body":"\n{{entity:rm-5}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-roadmap-8","title":"RM-6 Copies, the edge and the first site","level":2,"document":"doc-roadmap","order":8,"body":"\n{{entity:rm-6}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-roadmap-9","title":"RM-7 Agent plane","level":2,"document":"doc-roadmap","order":9,"body":"\n{{entity:rm-7}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-roadmap-10","title":"RM-8 Content features","level":2,"document":"doc-roadmap","order":10,"body":"\n{{entity:rm-8}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-roadmap-11","title":"RM-9 Cloud profile","level":2,"document":"doc-roadmap","order":11,"body":"\n{{entity:rm-9}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-glossary-1","title":"Glossary","level":1,"document":"doc-glossary","order":1,"body":"\nEach term is defined once and used with this meaning throughout the specification.\n\n{{entity:term-tenant}}\n\n{{entity:term-tenant-database}}\n\n{{entity:term-control-plane}}\n\n{{entity:term-tenant-directory}}\n\n{{entity:term-placement}}\n\n{{entity:term-realm}}\n\n{{entity:term-principal}}\n\n{{entity:term-sign-in-session}}\n\n{{entity:term-assertion}}\n\n{{entity:term-access-token}}\n\n{{entity:term-delegation}}\n\n{{entity:term-emailed-link}}\n\n{{entity:term-step-up}}\n\n{{entity:term-job}}\n\n{{entity:term-schedule}}\n\n{{entity:term-trigger}}\n\n{{entity:term-lease}}\n\n{{entity:term-fencing-token}}\n\n{{entity:term-idempotency-key}}\n\n{{entity:term-wake-index}}\n\n{{entity:term-workflow}}\n\n{{entity:term-connector}}\n\n{{entity:term-stored-copy}}\n\n{{entity:term-shared-copy}}\n\n{{entity:term-audience-class}}\n\n{{entity:term-freshness-bound}}\n\n{{entity:term-erasure-point}}\n\n{{entity:term-surrogate-key}}\n\n{{entity:term-edge-copy}}\n\n{{entity:term-operation}}\n\n{{entity:term-operation-catalogue}}\n\n{{entity:term-proposal}}\n\n{{entity:term-projection}}\n\n{{entity:term-audit-log}}\n\n{{entity:term-correlation-identifier}}\n\n{{entity:term-seam}}\n\n{{entity:term-adapter}}\n\n{{entity:term-tick}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-kernel-1","title":"Kernel","level":1,"document":"doc-kernel","order":1,"body":"\nThe kernel decides every domain question. These statements describe what it guarantees at its own interface, independent of storage and transport.\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-kernel-2","title":"Decisions","level":2,"document":"doc-kernel","order":2,"body":"\n{{entity:krn-001}}\n\n{{entity:krn-002}}\n\n{{entity:krn-003}}\n\n{{entity:krn-004}}\n\n{{entity:krn-005}}\n\n{{entity:krn-006}}\n\n{{entity:krn-007}}\n\n{{entity:krn-008}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-kernel-3","title":"Schema changes","level":2,"document":"doc-kernel","order":3,"body":"\n{{entity:krn-009}}\n\n{{entity:krn-010}}\n\n{{entity:krn-011}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-kernel-4","title":"Purity and proof","level":2,"document":"doc-kernel","order":4,"body":"\n{{entity:krn-012}}\n\n{{entity:krn-013}}\n\n{{entity:krn-014}}\n\n{{entity:krn-015}}\n\n{{entity:krn-016}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-storage-1","title":"Storage","level":1,"document":"doc-storage","order":1,"body":"\nThe store contract is the only way to a tenant database. An adapter is accepted by passing the conformance table, whatever database is behind it.\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-storage-2","title":"Adapters","level":2,"document":"doc-storage","order":2,"body":"\n{{entity:sto-001}}\n\n{{entity:sto-002}}\n\n{{entity:sto-003}}\n\n{{entity:sto-004}}\n\n{{entity:sto-005}}\n\n{{entity:sto-006}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-runtime-1","title":"Runtime, gateway and simulator","level":1,"document":"doc-runtime","order":1,"body":"\nThese statements describe behaviour the prototype already has. Each is tied to a test that exists, so the first milestone starts with a recorded passing run.\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-runtime-2","title":"Runtime","level":2,"document":"doc-runtime","order":2,"body":"\n{{entity:run-001}}\n\n{{entity:run-002}}\n\n{{entity:run-003}}\n\n{{entity:run-004}}\n\n{{entity:run-005}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-runtime-3","title":"Gateway","level":2,"document":"doc-runtime","order":3,"body":"\n{{entity:gwy-001}}\n\n{{entity:gwy-002}}\n\n{{entity:gwy-003}}\n\n{{entity:gwy-004}}\n\n{{entity:gwy-005}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-runtime-4","title":"Simulator","level":2,"document":"doc-runtime","order":4,"body":"\n{{entity:sim-001}}\n\n{{entity:sim-002}}\n\n{{entity:sim-003}}\n\n{{entity:sim-004}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-tenancy-1","title":"Tenancy","level":1,"document":"doc-tenancy","order":1,"body":"\nA tenant is a database, a file namespace, a realm and a key. The control plane creates, places, moves and removes them and holds nothing of their content.\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-tenancy-2","title":"Provisioning","level":2,"document":"doc-tenancy","order":2,"body":"\n{{entity:ten-001}}\n\n{{entity:ten-002}}\n\n{{entity:ten-003}}\n\n{{entity:ten-004}}\n\n{{entity:ten-005}}\n\n{{entity:ten-500}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-tenancy-3","title":"Isolation","level":2,"document":"doc-tenancy","order":3,"body":"\n{{entity:ten-006}}\n\n{{entity:ten-007}}\n\n{{entity:ten-008}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-tenancy-4","title":"Life cycle","level":2,"document":"doc-tenancy","order":4,"body":"\n{{entity:ten-009}}\n\n{{entity:ten-010}}\n\n{{entity:ten-011}}\n\n{{entity:ten-012}}\n\n{{entity:ten-013}}\n\n{{entity:ten-014}}\n\n{{entity:ten-015}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-identity-1","title":"Identity","level":1,"document":"doc-identity","order":1,"body":"\nThe identity service is the one place where credentials are handled. It answers one question for every other component: which principal, in which session, is making this request.\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-identity-2","title":"Sign-in methods","level":2,"document":"doc-identity","order":2,"body":"\n{{entity:idn-001}}\n\n{{entity:idn-002}}\n\n{{entity:idn-003}}\n\n{{entity:idn-004}}\n\n{{entity:idn-005}}\n\n{{entity:idn-006}}\n\n{{entity:idn-007}}\n\n{{entity:idn-008}}\n\n{{entity:idn-009}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-identity-3","title":"Sessions","level":2,"document":"doc-identity","order":3,"body":"\n{{entity:idn-010}}\n\n{{entity:idn-011}}\n\n{{entity:idn-012}}\n\n{{entity:idn-013}}\n\n{{entity:idn-014}}\n\n{{entity:idn-015}}\n\n{{entity:idn-016}}\n\n{{entity:idn-017}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-identity-4","title":"Factors, step-up and recovery","level":2,"document":"doc-identity","order":4,"body":"\n{{entity:idn-018}}\n\n{{entity:idn-019}}\n\n{{entity:idn-020}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-identity-5","title":"Record and presentation","level":2,"document":"doc-identity","order":5,"body":"\n{{entity:idn-021}}\n\n{{entity:idn-022}}\n\n{{entity:idn-023}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-federation-1","title":"Federation","level":1,"document":"doc-federation","order":1,"body":"\nA tenant can hand authentication of its people to its own identity provider. The platform is a relying party and a service provider, and treats everything a provider sends as input to be verified.\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-federation-2","title":"OpenID Connect","level":2,"document":"doc-federation","order":2,"body":"\n{{entity:fed-001}}\n\n{{entity:fed-002}}\n\n{{entity:fed-003}}\n\n{{entity:fed-004}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-federation-3","title":"SAML","level":2,"document":"doc-federation","order":3,"body":"\n{{entity:fed-005}}\n\n{{entity:fed-006}}\n\n{{entity:fed-007}}\n\n{{entity:fed-008}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-federation-4","title":"Policy and linking","level":2,"document":"doc-federation","order":4,"body":"\n{{entity:fed-009}}\n\n{{entity:fed-010}}\n\n{{entity:fed-011}}\n\n{{entity:fed-012}}\n\n{{entity:fed-013}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-federation-5","title":"Provisioning","level":2,"document":"doc-federation","order":5,"body":"\n{{entity:fed-014}}\n\n{{entity:fed-015}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-tokens-1","title":"Tokens","level":1,"document":"doc-tokens","order":1,"body":"\nCallers that are not browsers authenticate with signed access tokens. An agent is such a caller, and when it acts for a person the token says so.\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-tokens-2","title":"Issue","level":2,"document":"doc-tokens","order":2,"body":"\n{{entity:tok-001}}\n\n{{entity:tok-002}}\n\n{{entity:tok-003}}\n\n{{entity:tok-004}}\n\n{{entity:tok-005}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-tokens-3","title":"Verify and revoke","level":2,"document":"doc-tokens","order":3,"body":"\n{{entity:tok-006}}\n\n{{entity:tok-007}}\n\n{{entity:tok-008}}\n\n{{entity:tok-009}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-scheduling-1","title":"Scheduling","level":1,"document":"doc-scheduling","order":1,"body":"\nScheduled work is a record in the tenant database with a due time and an outcome. Workers find it through the wake index, hold it under a lease and report back with the token of that lease.\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-scheduling-2","title":"Due work","level":2,"document":"doc-scheduling","order":2,"body":"\n{{entity:sch-001}}\n\n{{entity:sch-002}}\n\n{{entity:sch-003}}\n\n{{entity:sch-004}}\n\n{{entity:sch-005}}\n\n{{entity:sch-006}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-scheduling-3","title":"Finding work","level":2,"document":"doc-scheduling","order":3,"body":"\n{{entity:sch-007}}\n\n{{entity:sch-008}}\n\n{{entity:sch-009}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-scheduling-4","title":"Failure","level":2,"document":"doc-scheduling","order":4,"body":"\n{{entity:sch-010}}\n\n{{entity:sch-011}}\n\n{{entity:sch-012}}\n\n{{entity:sch-013}}\n\n{{entity:sch-014}}\n\n{{entity:sch-015}}\n\n{{entity:sch-016}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-workflows-1","title":"Workflows","level":1,"document":"doc-workflows","order":1,"body":"\nA workflow is a state machine a tenant defines. The kernel decides each step, and adapters carry out what the step asks for after it commits.\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-workflows-2","title":"Definition and activation","level":2,"document":"doc-workflows","order":2,"body":"\n{{entity:wfl-001}}\n\n{{entity:wfl-002}}\n\n{{entity:wfl-003}}\n\n{{entity:wfl-004}}\n\n{{entity:wfl-005}}\n\n{{entity:wfl-006}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-workflows-3","title":"External effects","level":2,"document":"doc-workflows","order":3,"body":"\n{{entity:wfl-007}}\n\n{{entity:wfl-008}}\n\n{{entity:wfl-009}}\n\n{{entity:wfl-010}}\n\n{{entity:wfl-011}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-copies-1","title":"Stored copies","level":1,"document":"doc-copies","order":1,"body":"\nA stored copy is designed, not added. Each class of copy has an owner, a key, a freshness bound and an erasure point, and its key is built from the versions the answer was computed from.\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-copies-2","title":"Classes and keys","level":2,"document":"doc-copies","order":2,"body":"\n{{entity:cpy-001}}\n\n{{entity:cpy-002}}\n\n{{entity:cpy-003}}\n\n{{entity:cpy-004}}\n\n{{entity:cpy-005}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-copies-3","title":"Isolation","level":2,"document":"doc-copies","order":3,"body":"\n{{entity:cpy-006}}\n\n{{entity:cpy-007}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-copies-4","title":"Freshness and failure","level":2,"document":"doc-copies","order":4,"body":"\n{{entity:cpy-008}}\n\n{{entity:cpy-009}}\n\n{{entity:cpy-010}}\n\n{{entity:cpy-011}}\n\n{{entity:cpy-012}}\n\n{{entity:cpy-013}}\n\n{{entity:cpy-014}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-edge-1","title":"Edge","level":1,"document":"doc-edge","order":1,"body":"\nThe edge holds copies of public responses close to readers. Every such copy is keyed by host, labelled with what it was made from, and purged when that changes.\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-edge-2","title":"Storability","level":2,"document":"doc-edge","order":2,"body":"\n{{entity:edg-001}}\n\n{{entity:edg-002}}\n\n{{entity:edg-003}}\n\n{{entity:edg-004}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-edge-3","title":"Purge","level":2,"document":"doc-edge","order":3,"body":"\n{{entity:edg-005}}\n\n{{entity:edg-006}}\n\n{{entity:edg-007}}\n\n{{entity:edg-008}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-edge-4","title":"Domains and limits","level":2,"document":"doc-edge","order":4,"body":"\n{{entity:edg-009}}\n\n{{entity:edg-010}}\n\n{{entity:edg-011}}\n\n{{entity:edg-012}}\n\n{{entity:edg-013}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-agents-1","title":"Agent operation","level":1,"document":"doc-agents","order":1,"body":"\nAn agent is a principal like any other. What makes the platform operable by agents is that every capability is described, can be tried without effect, explains its refusals and leaves a record.\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-agents-2","title":"Discover","level":2,"document":"doc-agents","order":2,"body":"\n{{entity:agt-001}}\n\n{{entity:agt-002}}\n\n{{entity:agt-003}}\n\n{{entity:agt-004}}\n\n{{entity:agt-005}}\n\n{{entity:agt-006}}\n\n{{entity:agt-007}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-agents-3","title":"Try and explain","level":2,"document":"doc-agents","order":3,"body":"\n{{entity:agt-008}}\n\n{{entity:agt-009}}\n\n{{entity:agt-010}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-agents-4","title":"Propose and approve","level":2,"document":"doc-agents","order":4,"body":"\n{{entity:agt-011}}\n\n{{entity:agt-012}}\n\n{{entity:agt-013}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-agents-5","title":"Authorise, attribute and limit","level":2,"document":"doc-agents","order":5,"body":"\n{{entity:agt-014}}\n\n{{entity:agt-015}}\n\n{{entity:agt-016}}\n\n{{entity:agt-017}}\n\n{{entity:agt-500}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-observability-1","title":"Observability and audit","level":1,"document":"doc-observability","order":1,"body":"\nTelemetry says how the platform is behaving. The audit log says who did what. They are separate records with separate rules.\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-observability-2","title":"Telemetry","level":2,"document":"doc-observability","order":2,"body":"\n{{entity:obs-001}}\n\n{{entity:obs-002}}\n\n{{entity:obs-003}}\n\n{{entity:obs-004}}\n\n{{entity:obs-005}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-observability-3","title":"Audit","level":2,"document":"doc-observability","order":3,"body":"\n{{entity:obs-006}}\n\n{{entity:obs-007}}\n\n{{entity:obs-008}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-content-1","title":"Content","level":1,"document":"doc-content","order":1,"body":"\nContent is tenant data described by tenant metadata. The first four statements are met by the prototype, and the rest complete the model for editorial work.\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-content-2","title":"Model","level":2,"document":"doc-content","order":2,"body":"\n{{entity:cms-001}}\n\n{{entity:cms-002}}\n\n{{entity:cms-003}}\n\n{{entity:cms-004}}\n\n{{entity:cms-005}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-content-3","title":"Versions, media and languages","level":2,"document":"doc-content","order":3,"body":"\n{{entity:cms-006}}\n\n{{entity:cms-007}}\n\n{{entity:cms-008}}\n\n{{entity:cms-009}}\n\n{{entity:cms-010}}\n\n{{entity:cms-011}}\n\n{{entity:cms-012}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-platform-1","title":"Platform","level":1,"document":"doc-platform","order":1,"body":"\nThe platform is the same set of component images in two places: a compose file on one machine and a cloud profile. Everything that differs between them is an adapter behind a seam.\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-platform-2","title":"Local stack and seams","level":2,"document":"doc-platform","order":2,"body":"\n{{entity:dep-001}}\n\n{{entity:dep-002}}\n\n{{entity:dep-003}}\n\n{{entity:dep-004}}\n\n{{entity:dep-005}}\n\n{{entity:dep-006}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-platform-3","title":"Cloud profile","level":2,"document":"doc-platform","order":3,"body":"\n{{entity:dep-007}}\n\n{{entity:dep-008}}\n\n{{entity:dep-009}}\n\n{{entity:dep-010}}\n\n{{entity:dep-011}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-platform-4","title":"Keys and credentials","level":2,"document":"doc-platform","order":4,"body":"\n{{entity:sec-001}}\n\n{{entity:sec-002}}\n\n{{entity:sec-003}}\n\n{{entity:sec-004}}\n\n{{entity:sec-005}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-platform-5","title":"Assurance","level":2,"document":"doc-platform","order":5,"body":"\n{{entity:asr-001}}\n\n{{entity:asr-002}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-whitepaper-9","title":"Architecture review","level":2,"document":"doc-whitepaper","order":101,"body":"\nThe goals, constraints, decisions, boundaries, components and open questions that the architecture review adds. The requirements that trace to them are in [architecture](../09-architecture/architecture.md).\n\n**Goals**\n\n{{entity:g-100}}\n{{entity:g-101}}\n{{entity:g-102}}\n{{entity:g-103}}\n{{entity:g-104}}\n\n**Constraints**\n\n{{entity:k-100}}\n\n**Decisions**\n\n{{entity:d-100}}\n{{entity:d-101}}\n{{entity:d-102}}\n{{entity:d-103}}\n\n**Boundaries**\n\n{{entity:b-100}}\n{{entity:b-101}}\n\n**Components**\n\n{{entity:limit-store}}\n{{entity:backup-archive}}\n{{entity:fleet-reporting}}\n{{entity:product-module}}\n{{entity:external-endpoint}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-whitepaper-209","title":"Conversational interface review","level":2,"document":"doc-whitepaper","order":209,"body":"\nThe conversational interface and the authoring experience, seen from the person at the screen.\n\n**Goals**\n\n{{entity:g-200}}\n{{entity:g-201}}\n{{entity:g-202}}\n{{entity:g-203}}\n{{entity:g-204}}\n{{entity:g-205}}\n{{entity:g-206}}\n{{entity:g-207}}\n\n**Non-goals**\n\n{{entity:ng-200}}\n{{entity:ng-201}}\n{{entity:ng-202}}\n\n**Boundaries**\n\n{{entity:b-200}}\n{{entity:b-201}}\n{{entity:b-202}}\n\n**Components**\n\n{{entity:conversation-service}}\n{{entity:model-provider}}\n{{entity:local-model-adapter}}\n\n**Decisions**\n\n{{entity:d-200}}\n{{entity:d-201}}\n{{entity:d-202}}\n{{entity:d-203}}\n{{entity:d-204}}\n{{entity:d-205}}\n\n**Constraints**\n\n{{entity:k-200}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-arch-1","title":"Architecture","level":1,"document":"doc-architecture","order":1,"body":"\nThe requirements that the component model has to support and that the other documents do not state: what the platform does while the control plane is down, how notices and outbox events are delivered, how formats change while two versions run, how much one decision loads, which limits are shared, how tenants are backed up, and how a product module is added. Each requirement names the boundary it is observed at and the components that carry it.\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-arch-2","title":"Control plane and wake index","level":2,"document":"doc-architecture","order":2,"body":"\n{{entity:arc-100}}\n\n{{entity:arc-101}}\n\n{{entity:arc-500}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-arch-3","title":"Notices and outbox","level":2,"document":"doc-architecture","order":3,"body":"\n{{entity:arc-102}}\n\n{{entity:arc-103}}\n\n{{entity:arc-104}}\n\n{{entity:arc-105}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-arch-4","title":"Change across versions","level":2,"document":"doc-architecture","order":4,"body":"\n{{entity:arc-106}}\n\n{{entity:arc-107}}\n\n{{entity:arc-115}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-arch-5","title":"Kernel load, limits and connections","level":2,"document":"doc-architecture","order":5,"body":"\n{{entity:arc-108}}\n\n{{entity:arc-109}}\n\n{{entity:arc-114}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-arch-6","title":"Reporting and backup","level":2,"document":"doc-architecture","order":6,"body":"\n{{entity:arc-110}}\n\n{{entity:arc-111}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-arch-7","title":"Extension","level":2,"document":"doc-architecture","order":7,"body":"\n{{entity:arc-112}}\n\n{{entity:arc-113}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-index-1","title":"Specification","level":1,"document":"doc-index","order":1,"body":"\nRequirements derived from [the white paper](00-vision/whitepaper.md), in the format Concordance lints. Each one names the boundary it is observed at, what it traces to, how it is proved and the milestone at which it is first verified. Case tables live beside their file, in `cases/`.\n\n| File | Prefix | Covers |\n|---|---|---|\n| [01-core/kernel.md](01-core/kernel.md) | KRN | The pure transition function, its invariants and the abstract model |\n| [01-core/storage.md](01-core/storage.md) | STO | The store contract and its adapters |\n| [01-core/runtime.md](01-core/runtime.md) | RUN, GWY, SIM | What the existing services and the simulator guarantee today |\n| [02-tenancy/tenancy.md](02-tenancy/tenancy.md) | TEN | The control plane, the tenant directory and the life of a tenant |\n| [03-identity/identity.md](03-identity/identity.md) | IDN | Realms, sign-in methods, sessions, factors and recovery |\n| [03-identity/federation.md](03-identity/federation.md) | FED | OpenID Connect, SAML and SCIM |\n| [03-identity/tokens.md](03-identity/tokens.md) | TOK | Service accounts, agent identities, delegation and signing keys |\n| [04-automation/scheduling.md](04-automation/scheduling.md) | SCH | Jobs, schedules, triggers and leases |\n| [04-automation/workflows.md](04-automation/workflows.md) | WFL | Workflows as metadata, connectors and scheduled publication |\n| [05-delivery/copies.md](05-delivery/copies.md) | CPY | How data is kept outside its owner for cheaper reads, and how it stays right |\n| [05-delivery/edge.md](05-delivery/edge.md) | EDG | The content delivery network, domains, certificates and limits |\n| [06-agents/operations.md](06-agents/operations.md) | AGT | The operation catalogue, dry runs, proposals and limits on agents |\n| [06-agents/observability.md](06-agents/observability.md) | OBS | Telemetry, correlation, health and the audit log |\n| [06-agents/safety.md](06-agents/safety.md) | AGS | Agent safety and governance: untrusted text, delegation, blast radius, platform-operating agents, data leaving the platform and concurrent change |\n| [07-content/content.md](07-content/content.md) | CMS | Content types, versions, media, languages and preview |\n| [08-platform/platform.md](08-platform/platform.md) | DEP, SEC, ASR | The local stack, the cloud profile, keys and the assurance loop |\n| [09-privacy/privacy.md](09-privacy/privacy.md) | PRV | Data subject rights, sealing, retention and legal hold, residency, consent, platform access and compliance evidence |\n| [09-operations/reliability.md](09-operations/reliability.md) | OPS | Reference load, admission, retries, failure containment, data safety, releases, objectives, alerts and runbooks |\n| [09-threat/threat-model.md](09-threat/threat-model.md) | THR | The attack classes that cut across components: response headers, transport, reachability, supply chain, incidents and abuse |\n| [09-conversation/conversation.md](09-conversation/conversation.md) | CNV | The conversational interface: the assistant, previews and confirmations, explanations, the model provider and onboarding |\n| [09-conversation/authoring.md](09-conversation/authoring.md) | UXA | Empty, failing, unsaved, shared and expired states of the authoring application and sign-in pages, and reader throttling |\n| [09-administration/administration.md](09-administration/administration.md) | ADM | Roles, teams, invitations, sandbox and staging tenants, offboarding and support access |\n| [02-tenancy/billing.md](02-tenancy/billing.md) | BIL | Plans, quotas, trials, metering, the billing export and published objectives |\n| [04-automation/notifications.md](04-automation/notifications.md) | NTF | Subscriptions, email and inbox notices, approval tasks |\n| [04-automation/integrations.md](04-automation/integrations.md) | INT | Inbound and outbound webhooks, the trigger and action catalogue, installed templates |\n| [07-content/forms.md](07-content/forms.md) | FRM | Form submissions: storage, tokens, notices, retention and export |\n| [07-content/search.md](07-content/search.md) | SRH | Search over published and draft content, limited by audience |\n| [09-architecture/architecture.md](09-architecture/architecture.md) | ARC | The control plane's availability, notices and outbox, change across versions, kernel load, shared limits, reporting, backup and extension |\n| [07-content/content-tokens.md](07-content/content-tokens.md) | CTK | Tenant-defined tokens: definition, evaluation, output contexts, stored copies and email |\n| [04-automation/email.md](04-automation/email.md) | EML | The mail contract and its adapters, sending, sender domains, suppression and the mail log |\n| [02-tenancy/tenant-migrations.md](02-tenancy/tenant-migrations.md) | MIG | Tenant migrations: the guarantee a tenant keeps through its own changes, platform changes and moves, the conversions, imports and exports that carry them |\n| [08-platform/release-lifecycle.md](08-platform/release-lifecycle.md) | REL | Release lifecycle: image digests, stage and production environments and parity, promotion and approval, colour switches, rollback and the release records |\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-whitepaper-150","title":"Product review","level":2,"document":"doc-whitepaper","order":150,"body":"\nWhat a customer can buy, what the first release left out, and the decisions that follow from it.\n\n**Goals**\n\n{{entity:g-150}}\n\n{{entity:g-151}}\n\n{{entity:g-152}}\n\n{{entity:g-153}}\n\n{{entity:g-154}}\n\n{{entity:g-155}}\n\n{{entity:g-156}}\n\n{{entity:g-157}}\n\n{{entity:g-158}}\n\n{{entity:g-159}}\n\n{{entity:g-160}}\n\n{{entity:g-161}}\n\n{{entity:g-162}}\n\n{{entity:g-163}}\n\n{{entity:g-164}}\n\n{{entity:g-165}}\n\n{{entity:g-166}}\n\n{{entity:g-167}}\n\n{{entity:g-168}}\n\n**Non-goals**\n\n{{entity:ng-150}}\n\n{{entity:ng-151}}\n\n{{entity:ng-152}}\n\n{{entity:ng-153}}\n\n{{entity:ng-154}}\n\n{{entity:ng-155}}\n\n**Boundaries**\n\n{{entity:b-150}}\n\n{{entity:b-151}}\n\n{{entity:b-152}}\n\n{{entity:b-153}}\n\n{{entity:b-154}}\n\n{{entity:b-155}}\n\n{{entity:b-156}}\n\n**Decisions**\n\n{{entity:d-150}}\n\n{{entity:d-151}}\n\n{{entity:d-152}}\n\n{{entity:d-153}}\n\n{{entity:d-154}}\n\n**Components**\n\n{{entity:search-index}}\n\n{{entity:notification-service}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-glossary-150","title":"Product review terms","level":2,"document":"doc-glossary","order":150,"body":"\nThe terms that the product review introduces.\n\n{{entity:term-sandbox-tenant}}\n\n{{entity:term-staging-tenant}}\n\n{{entity:term-environment}}\n\n{{entity:term-draft}}\n\n{{entity:term-preview-link}}\n\n{{entity:term-delivery-key}}\n\n{{entity:term-support-grant}}\n\n{{entity:term-notice}}\n\n{{entity:term-inbox}}\n\n{{entity:term-plan}}\n\n{{entity:term-quota}}\n\n{{entity:term-webhook}}\n\n{{entity:term-redirect}}\n\n{{entity:term-submission}}\n\n{{entity:term-search-index}}\n\n{{entity:term-archive}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-administration-1","title":"Administration","level":1,"document":"doc-administration","order":1,"body":"\nThe people, roles and tenants of an organisation, the life of a tenant from a sandbox to its deletion, and the support access that platform operators have to a tenant.\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-administration-2","title":"Roles and teams","level":2,"document":"doc-administration","order":2,"body":"\n{{entity:adm-150}}\n\n{{entity:adm-151}}\n\n{{entity:adm-152}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-administration-3","title":"Invitations and onboarding","level":2,"document":"doc-administration","order":3,"body":"\n{{entity:adm-153}}\n\n{{entity:adm-154}}\n\n{{entity:adm-155}}\n\n{{entity:adm-156}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-administration-4","title":"Tenant kinds and environments","level":2,"document":"doc-administration","order":4,"body":"\n{{entity:adm-157}}\n\n{{entity:adm-158}}\n\n{{entity:adm-159}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-administration-5","title":"Offboarding","level":2,"document":"doc-administration","order":5,"body":"\n{{entity:adm-160}}\n\n{{entity:adm-161}}\n\n{{entity:adm-162}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-administration-6","title":"Support access","level":2,"document":"doc-administration","order":6,"body":"\n{{entity:adm-163}}\n\n{{entity:adm-164}}\n\n{{entity:adm-165}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-billing-1","title":"Plans, metering and billing","level":1,"document":"doc-billing","order":1,"body":"\nA plan states the quotas and trial terms of a tenant. The platform counts metered use and exports it to the billing system the tenant names. It does not charge anyone.\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-billing-2","title":"Plans and quotas","level":2,"document":"doc-billing","order":2,"body":"\n{{entity:bil-150}}\n\n{{entity:bil-151}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-billing-3","title":"Trials","level":2,"document":"doc-billing","order":3,"body":"\n{{entity:bil-154}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-billing-4","title":"Metering and export","level":2,"document":"doc-billing","order":4,"body":"\n{{entity:bil-152}}\n\n{{entity:bil-153}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-billing-5","title":"Published objectives","level":2,"document":"doc-billing","order":5,"body":"\n{{entity:bil-155}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-notifications-1","title":"Notifications and inbox","level":1,"document":"doc-notifications","order":1,"body":"\nSubscriptions turn events into notices. A notice goes by email, into the inbox of the person it names, or both, and carries only what its recipient is permitted to read.\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-notifications-2","title":"Notices and inbox","level":2,"document":"doc-notifications","order":2,"body":"\n{{entity:ntf-150}}\n\n{{entity:ntf-151}}\n\n{{entity:ntf-152}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-integrations-1","title":"Integrations and webhooks","level":1,"document":"doc-integrations","order":1,"body":"\nOther systems reach a tenant's workflows through signed webhooks, and a tenant sees what its own webhooks did. Templates and integrations that the platform publishes are installed after review.\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-integrations-2","title":"Inbound webhooks","level":2,"document":"doc-integrations","order":2,"body":"\n{{entity:int-150}}\n\n{{entity:int-151}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-integrations-3","title":"Outbound deliveries and the catalogue","level":2,"document":"doc-integrations","order":3,"body":"\n{{entity:int-152}}\n\n{{entity:int-153}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-integrations-4","title":"Installed templates and integrations","level":2,"document":"doc-integrations","order":4,"body":"\n{{entity:int-154}}\n\n{{entity:int-155}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-forms-1","title":"Forms and submissions","level":1,"document":"doc-forms","order":1,"body":"\nA form on a tenant's site collects submissions. A submission is a record of the tenant, stored before the reader is answered, notified through the tenant's subscriptions and erased when its retention period ends.\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-forms-2","title":"Submissions","level":2,"document":"doc-forms","order":2,"body":"\n{{entity:frm-150}}\n\n{{entity:frm-151}}\n\n{{entity:frm-152}}\n\n{{entity:frm-154}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-search-1","title":"Search","level":1,"document":"doc-search","order":1,"body":"\nSearch answers readers and editors from the tenant's own search index, and returns only what the reader or editor is permitted to see.\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-search-2","title":"Queries","level":2,"document":"doc-search","order":2,"body":"\n{{entity:srh-150}}\n\n{{entity:srh-151}}\n\n{{entity:srh-152}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-content-150","title":"Authoring","level":2,"document":"doc-content","order":150,"body":"\nA content type declares its fields with one of the types text, rich text, number, date, boolean, choice, reference or media. Records of a type are created and edited as drafts, and readers see a change only when it is published.\n\n{{entity:cms-150}}\n\n{{entity:cms-151}}\n\n{{entity:cms-152}}\n\n{{entity:cms-153}}\n\n{{entity:cms-154}}\n\n{{entity:cms-155}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-content-151","title":"Review and publication","level":2,"document":"doc-content","order":151,"body":"\nA tenant can mark a content type for review. Approval is a workflow step with a named approver.\n\n{{entity:cms-156}}\n\n{{entity:cms-157}}\n\n{{entity:cms-158}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-content-152","title":"Preview links","level":2,"document":"doc-content","order":152,"body":"\nA preview link is an expiring address for one draft. It is the reviewer's view of the draft, and nothing more.\n\n{{entity:cms-159}}\n\n{{entity:cms-160}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-content-153","title":"Addresses and redirects","level":2,"document":"doc-content","order":153,"body":"\n{{entity:cms-161}}\n\n{{entity:cms-162}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-content-154","title":"Delivery interface","level":2,"document":"doc-content","order":154,"body":"\nThe delivery interface serves published content to tenant applications and to the reader site. Its named queries and views are tenant metadata.\n\n{{entity:cms-163}}\n\n{{entity:cms-164}}\n\n{{entity:cms-165}}\n\n{{entity:cms-166}}\n\n{{entity:cms-167}}\n\n{{entity:cms-168}}\n\n{{entity:cms-169}}\n\n{{entity:cms-170}}\n\n{{entity:cms-171}}\n\n{{entity:cms-173}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-content-155","title":"Import and export","level":2,"document":"doc-content","order":155,"body":"\n{{entity:cms-172}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-edge-150","title":"Discovery","level":2,"document":"doc-edge","order":150,"body":"\n{{entity:edg-150}}\n\n{{entity:edg-151}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-scheduling-150","title":"Bulk work","level":2,"document":"doc-scheduling","order":150,"body":"\n{{entity:sch-150}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-observability-150","title":"Status","level":2,"document":"doc-observability","order":150,"body":"\n{{entity:obs-150}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-conversation-1","title":"Conversation","level":1,"document":"doc-conversation","order":1,"body":"\nThe conversation is a second way into the operations that the authoring application already calls. The assistant acts for one person with that person's permissions, and every change it proposes is shown as a preview before it is applied. The requirements here make the conversation a surface of the platform, not a chat window placed beside it.\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-conversation-2","title":"Operations and authority","level":2,"document":"doc-conversation","order":2,"body":"\nWhat the assistant may call, and whose permissions it uses.\n\n{{entity:cnv-200}}\n\n{{entity:cnv-201}}\n\n{{entity:cnv-202}}\n\n{{entity:cnv-203}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-conversation-3","title":"Preview and confirmation","level":2,"document":"doc-conversation","order":3,"body":"\nNothing the assistant does reaches a record before the person has seen it and said yes.\n\n{{entity:cnv-205}}\n\n{{entity:cnv-206}}\n\n{{entity:cnv-207}}\n\n{{entity:cnv-208}}\n\n{{entity:cnv-209}}\n\n{{entity:cnv-210}}\n\n{{entity:cnv-211}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-conversation-4","title":"Explanation and evidence","level":2,"document":"doc-conversation","order":4,"body":"\nEvery answer about tenant data says where it came from.\n\n{{entity:cnv-212}}\n\n{{entity:cnv-213}}\n\n{{entity:cnv-214}}\n\n{{entity:cnv-215}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-conversation-5","title":"One interface","level":2,"document":"doc-conversation","order":5,"body":"\nThe conversation and the authoring application show the same views and share the selection.\n\n{{entity:cnv-216}}\n\n{{entity:cnv-217}}\n\n{{entity:cnv-218}}\n\n{{entity:cnv-219}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-conversation-6","title":"Replies, streams and cancellation","level":2,"document":"doc-conversation","order":6,"body":"\nA reply streams, can be stopped, and survives a reload.\n\n{{entity:cnv-220}}\n\n{{entity:cnv-221}}\n\n{{entity:cnv-222}}\n\n{{entity:cnv-223}}\n\n{{entity:cnv-224}}\n\n{{entity:cnv-225}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-conversation-7","title":"Records, retention and visibility","level":2,"document":"doc-conversation","order":7,"body":"\nA conversation is tenant data, with the same retention, erasure and attribution as any other.\n\n{{entity:cnv-226}}\n\n{{entity:cnv-227}}\n\n{{entity:cnv-228}}\n\n{{entity:cnv-229}}\n\n{{entity:cnv-230}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-conversation-8","title":"Model provider","level":2,"document":"doc-conversation","order":8,"body":"\nThe model is a seam. Its adapters are accepted by conformance, and tenant policy governs what it receives.\n\n{{entity:cnv-231}}\n\n{{entity:cnv-232}}\n\n{{entity:cnv-233}}\n\n{{entity:cnv-234}}\n\n{{entity:cnv-235}}\n\n{{entity:cnv-236}}\n\n{{entity:cnv-500}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-conversation-9","title":"Accessibility, network and language","level":2,"document":"doc-conversation","order":9,"body":"\nThe conversation works with assistive technology, on small screens, on poor networks and in the person's language.\n\n{{entity:cnv-237}}\n\n{{entity:cnv-238}}\n\n{{entity:cnv-239}}\n\n{{entity:cnv-240}}\n\n{{entity:cnv-241}}\n\n{{entity:cnv-242}}\n\n{{entity:cnv-243}}\n\n{{entity:cnv-244}}\n\n{{entity:cnv-245}}\n\n{{entity:cnv-246}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-conversation-10","title":"Onboarding","level":2,"document":"doc-conversation","order":10,"body":"\nA new tenant is set up by conversation, through the same previews and confirmations.\n\n{{entity:cnv-247}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-conversation-11","title":"Untrusted content","level":2,"document":"doc-conversation","order":11,"body":"\nWhere the person can tell what came from outside the tenant.\n\n{{entity:cnv-248}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-authoring-1","title":"Authoring experience","level":1,"document":"doc-authoring","order":1,"body":"\nThe authoring application and the sign-in pages are where people do most of their work by hand. The requirements here cover the states a person meets when something is empty, failing, unsaved, shared, expired or slow.\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-authoring-2","title":"Empty states, errors and sign-in","level":2,"document":"doc-authoring","order":2,"body":"\nEach state says what it holds, or what to do next.\n\n{{entity:uxa-200}}\n\n{{entity:uxa-201}}\n\n{{entity:uxa-202}}\n\n{{entity:uxa-203}}\n\n{{entity:uxa-213}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-authoring-3","title":"Drafts, saves and conflicts","level":2,"document":"doc-authoring","order":3,"body":"\nWork is kept until it is saved, and two people's changes are not overwritten silently.\n\n{{entity:uxa-204}}\n\n{{entity:uxa-205}}\n\n{{entity:uxa-206}}\n\n{{entity:uxa-207}}\n\n{{entity:uxa-208}}\n\n{{entity:uxa-209}}\n\n{{entity:uxa-210}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-authoring-4","title":"Sessions, destructive actions and layout","level":2,"document":"doc-authoring","order":4,"body":"\nThe rest of the states a person meets while editing.\n\n{{entity:uxa-211}}\n\n{{entity:uxa-212}}\n\n{{entity:uxa-214}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-authoring-5","title":"Reader states","level":2,"document":"doc-authoring","order":5,"body":"\nWhat a reader sees when the platform refuses a request.\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-whitepaper-250","title":"Application security review","level":2,"document":"doc-whitepaper","order":250,"body":"\nThe attack classes a hostile tenant, a hostile visitor or a stolen credential could use, and the goals, constraints, decisions, boundaries and components that the requirements of the review depend on.\n\n**Goals**\n\n{{entity:g-250}}\n{{entity:g-251}}\n{{entity:g-252}}\n{{entity:g-253}}\n{{entity:g-254}}\n{{entity:g-255}}\n{{entity:g-256}}\n{{entity:g-257}}\n{{entity:g-258}}\n{{entity:g-259}}\n{{entity:g-260}}\n{{entity:g-261}}\n{{entity:g-262}}\n{{entity:g-263}}\n{{entity:g-264}}\n{{entity:g-265}}\n{{entity:g-266}}\n{{entity:g-267}}\n\n**Constraints**\n\n{{entity:k-250}}\n{{entity:k-251}}\n{{entity:k-252}}\n\n**Decisions**\n\n{{entity:d-250}}\n{{entity:d-251}}\n{{entity:d-252}}\n{{entity:d-253}}\n{{entity:d-254}}\n\n**Boundaries**\n\n{{entity:b-250}}\n{{entity:b-251}}\n{{entity:b-252}}\n\n**Components**\n\n{{entity:operator-console}}\n{{entity:outbound-gate}}\n{{entity:upload-scanner}}\n\n"},
    {"id":"sec-identity-250","title":"Guessing and enumeration","level":2,"document":"doc-identity","order":250,"body":"\n{{entity:idn-250}}\n\n{{entity:idn-251}}\n\n{{entity:idn-252}}\n\n{{entity:idn-253}}\n\n{{entity:idn-254}}\n\n{{entity:idn-255}}\n\n{{entity:idn-256}}\n\n{{entity:idn-257}}\n\n{{entity:idn-258}}\n\n"},
